module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.readback_ordered_only_by_statement_position

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }

data readback_ordered_only_by_statement_position: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "readback_ordered_only_by_statement_position" as NonEmptyStr,

  receipts: [
    "**a readback is written after the effect it must follow and has no dependency edge to it, so nothing in the program says it comes after** (INVALID STATE: an effectful producer and an observation of its consequence are both bound in one function, the observation appearing later in the text, and the author reads that position as sequence. The substrate is a dependency graph: what orders two nodes is an EDGE, and a reading whose inputs do not include the effect's result has none. The order it actually runs in is then decided by the evaluation strategy of whatever is executing it, which is not a property of the program.)",

    "WHAT IS AND IS NOT CLAIMED HERE, MEASURED RATHER THAN ASSUMED. The seed interpreter is EAGER: v1_interpreter eval_call evaluates every argument node before the call, unconditionally and in order, and a block's lets likewise. So under the seed, position DOES order these today and no wrong reading has been observed from this class. That is exactly why it is worth a row: the correctness rests on the executor's strategy rather than on the graph, it is invisible while that strategy holds, and the corpus is migrating toward emitted realizations and a demand engine (docs/plans/demand-engine-program.md) where a value nobody demands need not be computed when its neighbour was. A guarantee that holds because of how today's interpreter happens to walk the tree is the kind of guarantee DESIGN section 4b calls mitigatable at best -- and this one is not even written down, so nothing would notice it lapsing.",

    "WHY IT IS NOT THE WALL-CLOCK SIBLING. [[collector_armed_after_the_transition_it_observes]] is an instrument started at the wrong MOMENT by a human or a script, and its repair is to arm the collector first. [[enforcement_gate_positioned_after_the_effect_it_guards]] is a refusal computed before and enforced after. This one is neither: the author DID write the observation after the effect, and would pass a reading of the code, because the defect is that writing it after is not saying anything in this language. The two siblings are about WHEN something ran; this is about a language in which when is not expressed by where.",

    "DISTINGUISHING FACTS. Every value is correct in isolation and every type checks. The effect happens and the observation happens; the fault is that nothing relates them. The tell is a function that binds an effectful call and one or more readings whose arguments are all derived from the FUNCTION'S OWN PARAMETERS rather than from the effect's result -- an identity, a slot, a path, a slice name. A second tell is a record literal whose fields are one effect and several observations of it: the fields of a record have no order at all, so a reader looking for sequence there is reading punctuation.",

    "SPECIMEN, found 2026-09-20 in an UNLANDED fold of the microVM slot lane, described by shape because it does not resolve on main at the moment this row lands (gunbc.recurring_failure_mode unlanded_citation_indistinguishable_at_the_citing_end): the fold that produces every teardown verdict there. It binds the stop's outcome and then builds one ObservedTeardown (gunbc.runner_microvm_lifecycle, which does resolve) whose `cgroup`, `mounts`, `attempt_storage` and `credential_disk` fields call readbacks whose arguments are all derived from the bound attempt -- the slice, the jail root, the attempt directory, the credential device -- and none of which is `outcome`. THE SPECIMEN IS WEAKER THAN IT FIRST READS, AND THE CORRECTION IS THE INSTRUCTIVE PART. The record sits in the CONTINUATION of the stop's own bind, and gunbc.plans.demand_engine_program rules that Bind orders later computation after its value, so that enclosing bind DOES order these readbacks after the stop, and the mirror InvocationID read is bound before it. The fields are unordered RELATIVE TO EACH OTHER, which is harmless here because none of them writes. So this fold is not an instance of the invalid state; it is where the class was noticed. A realization that moved those readbacks across that bind would be violating Bind's ruled semantics -- a realization-conformance defect -- rather than exposing a missing program edge. THE INVALID STATE THIS ROW NAMES is the shape with NO enclosing bind and no data edge: sibling components of one product, or two sibling effects, where the effect and the observation of its subject are related by nothing but the order somebody wrote them in.",

    "THE CONSEQUENCE IF THE ORDER EVER CHANGES IS NOT SUBTLE, WHICH IS WHY A ROW RATHER THAN A NOTE. A cgroup read taken before the stop is a perfectly well-formed CgroupSubtreePopulated, so the cell quarantines for residue the stop was about to remove; a resource read before the guest created it is a perfectly well-formed ResourceAbsent, so the cell is RELEASED. Neither refuses, neither looks like a defect in the readback, and the wet receipt that passed under the old order stays on the branch as evidence that it all worked.",

    "THE REPAIR IS AN EDGE, AND THE EDGE IS ALSO THE SENTENCE. The stop is bound first and its ObservedStop is passed to every readback as a parameter named `after`. The readbacks do not otherwise consult it; the sequencing IS the use, and it is the only mechanism a dependency graph affords for it. A parameter that exists to order is not a decoration: in this substrate it is the word `after`, and removing it removes the ordering rather than removing noise.",

    "RECOGNITION RULE, cheap and mechanical: for every observation whose meaning depends on an effect, ask which of its arguments could not have been computed before that effect ran. If the answer is none, it is not ordered after it. The question is asked of ARGUMENTS, not of line numbers, and it is the same question whether the two sit in one record literal, one block, or two functions.",

    "RUNG FOUND AT: mitigatable -- caught by an author re-deriving the slice, before any execution. CEILING: structurally guaranteed. Whether an observation is causally downstream of an effect is decidable from the graph the compiler already holds: an effectful node and an observation of a subject that effect writes, with no path between them, is a refusable shape. What is missing is the SUBJECT relation -- the compiler knows the bounded stop is effectful and knows the cgroup-subtree read is effectful, and does not know they concern the same cell. NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER, at capability grain: effect subjects are modeled, so an effect declares what it writes and an observation declares what it reads, and the compiler refuses an unordered pair over one subject. Until that exists the wall is authorship and review, which is the rung this row claims and no higher.",
  ],

  evidence: [],
}
